; A lot sold over several postings, each at its own price, balances at
; its lot basis: every posting books the gain between basis and price
; exactly, and the transaction must balance within EUR's two places.
; Rounding each posting's gain to two places before summing let the
; errors add up, so these sales were rejected by a cent.  The gains
; below are what 3.4.1 and beancount accept.

2018-09-24 * Sold
    Assets:Current                                     92836.79 EUR
    Income:Capital gains                              -38525.84 EUR
    Assets:Investments       -1391 FOO {21.802871170463472 EUR} [2018-09-24] @ 37.2680 EUR
    Assets:Investments       -1100 FOO {21.802871170463472 EUR} [2018-09-24] @ 37.2700 EUR

2018-09-24 * Sold FOO
    Assets:Current                            633.56 EUR
    Income:Capital gains                     -262.91 EUR
    Assets:Investments       -13 FOO {21.802871170463472 EUR} [2018-09-24] @ 37.2680 EUR
    Assets:Investments        -4 FOO {21.802871170463472 EUR} [2018-09-24] @ 37.2700 EUR

test bal
        93470.35 EUR
           -2508 FOO  Assets
        93470.35 EUR    Current
           -2508 FOO    Investments
       -38788.75 EUR  Income:Capital gains
--------------------
        54681.60 EUR
           -2508 FOO
end test

; Each sale posting carries its lot basis, quantity times lot price, as
; its cost.
test reg --basis Investments
